# The shell scripts under linux/ are checked out on Ubuntu and run by /bin/sh. They are
# authored on Windows, and a CRLF checkout makes the kernel read the shebang as
# "/bin/sh\r" -- the script dies with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory", which
# says nothing about line endings. Pin them to LF regardless of core.autocrlf.
linux/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is fine either way, but keep the Windows tooling on CRLF explicitly rather
# than at the mercy of whoever cloned it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
